ait, but earlier thought was 0.08 for 2050. Let me adjust that to stay within 0.08. That would look like 0.01, 0.02, 0.05, 0.08, 0.15? Wait no, need to keep non-decreasing, so each step must be equal or higher than previous. Maybe adjust 2050 to 0.15. So the sequence would be 0.01, 0.02, 0.05, 0.08, 0.15. That's non-decreasing and each year further has higher probability.\n\nBut also, the overall chance might be low. Considering how tough these problems are, even with AI, it's a maybe. So finalizing the probabilities, ensuring each increases. Let me structure the JSON accordingly.\n</think>\n\n{\"2026\": 0.01, \"2030\": 0.02, \"2035\": 0.05, \"2040\": 0.08, \"2050\": 0.15}",
